  "_comment": {
    "about": "The Next.js half of the Polaris lending SDK. Top-level installs go to every host that composes it: the staff back office (app/handson/all/lending), the public quote page (app/portal/loan-quote) and, since 1.6.0, the borrower area (app/loans, app/actions/lending, app/api/lending, components/custom/lending), with the lending-owned plumbing that used to be borrowed from the RokctAI_frontend host (app/services/all/lending/base.ts over base_sdk's platformCall, app/actions/handson/all/lending/access.ts over api.lending.get_my_lending_access, currency.ts, lookups.ts, app/lib/lending/ncr_calculator.ts and reports_config.ts). The app_type.polaris block is the Polaris web app (Ray, 2026-10-17: a Next.js frontend that gets its landing from the SDK as the home SDK, staff do their thing when signed in as such, customers do what they do in the Dart app): it owns app/page.tsx (signed out to /landing; signed in to /handson/all/lending for staff, /loans for everyone else) and fills base_sdk's landing registries with one module each. The contract is polaris/docs/web-app.md. The shell is the protocol template core/utils/nextjs/composer/polaris.json (telemetry_sdk, base_sdk, auth_sdk, corporate_sdk, polaris_sdk as home_sdk).",
    "integrations": "The top-level line targets the RokctAI_frontend host's app/handson/sidebar-client.tsx; a host without that file skips it. The back office's own layout.tsx carries its navigation.",
    "app_type": "polaris: the home SDK's files and its one line at each of base_sdk's landing registries (hero-copy, hero-form, header-menu, site-metadata, plans-query, page-sections). polaris-plans-query.ts answers null: the Subscription Plan catalog is what a lender buys, so a borrower's landing lists none."
  }
